  "body": "Split from #330's reopen report (PR #603 fixed the reachable-controls part).\n\n1. **Angle Apply:** the Part alignment row's typed-angle **Apply** turns the part about its bounds centre, so the part moves relative to the WCS origin. The maintainer's report said the alignment \"shifts the model relative to the origin\". Decide the pivot: the WCS origin, the bounds centre, or a choice, record it, and make the row say which.\n2. **Default Flip:** unflipped currently means the picked face's outside points along +axis, so a face picked on G17 lays outside-up with the part below the plane. Users probably expect the picked face to become the bottom (face-down onto the table). Consider flipping the default; this is the maintainer's call.\n3. **Structural test:** `setup_page_alignment_rows_structure` asserts the controls are inside the window, not the properties pane rect. Tighten it to the pane rect, so a control spilling past the pane edge (the #330 bug) fails the test.\n\n**Done means:** each item is decided and recorded, with tests where behaviour changes.",
